 **Verifiability.** Publish the account architecture and recovery flow, get a third-party audit, and run a public bounty with a clear scope. The bounty could test whether funds protected by independent signing rules can move without additional authorization when a test phone is compromised. Recovery guardians and day-to-day signing limits serve different purposes. Publish which circumstances each test covers.
 
-**Demonstrability.** Show users how recovery on a new iPhone works and how an account can operate without generating a 12-word phrase. Aim for **90 seconds** in a device migration drill. When an app detects a visible signal such as jailbreaking, it can warn the user and point them to a new-account migration process from a trusted device.
+**A recovery users can see.** Demonstrate recovery on a new iPhone with an account that never generates a 12-word phrase. Aim for **90 seconds** in a device migration drill. When an app detects a visible signal such as jailbreaking, it can warn the user and point them to a new-account migration process from a trusted device.
 
 **Operational responsibility.** Users will contact support if they lose their iCloud account, delete a passkey, lose access to a guardian, or switch from iPhone to Android. They will also ask about responsibility and reimbursement after failed recovery. Launching accounts with passkeys and guardians calls for funding both the recovery process and the support team. A widespread recovery failure would damage the security commitment.
 
