 ## Conclusion
 
-DarkSword exposed the limits of hiding keys on a device. Encryption at rest still protects files. Using keys or a backup password on a phone requires a trusted execution environment. Apple supplies system protections. Trust Wallet can decide how users authorize actions and recover accounts.
+DarkSword exposed the limits of hiding keys on a device. Encryption at rest still protects files. Using keys or a backup password still requires a trustworthy device. Apple supplies system protections. Trust Wallet can decide how users authorize actions and recover accounts.
 
 SWIFT and Barz provide the smart account and passkey foundations. The next steps are making accounts without a single exportable seed the default, giving users recovery drills, and publishing verifiable commitments on recovery success and time. This is a way for Trust Wallet to differentiate itself from Phantom's emphasis on ease of use and Coinbase's compliance brand.
 
-**Give priority in the additional iOS budget to seedless accounts and verifiable recovery.** If Trust Wallet takes just one step, make seedless setup the default for new users on supported networks, with a trusted way to restore access.
+**Put the next iOS security dollars into seedless accounts and verifiable recovery.** If Trust Wallet takes just one step, make seedless setup the default for new users on supported networks, with a trusted way to restore access.
